   "overview": "Twelve pitches, an old-school classic that made the first direct attempt on Mount Morrison's huge north face, following a big gully system. Given the rock, lead it only as an experienced trad climber comfortable a couple of grades above the rating. Lower down, a dihedral and a gully lead to the buttress crest. A red chimney near the top is loaded with big, dangerous blocks; belay before it. Rappel 40' behind the notch, then 400' of class 3 to the summit.",
